      "relative_path": "neurophysiology/NEURO_interoception_insular_cortex.md",
      "headings": [
        "# Interoception and the Insular Cortex in Bodily Self-Awareness",
        "## Abstract",
        "## Physiological Mechanisms",
        "### Interoceptive Pathways",
        "### Insular Cortex Architecture",
        "### Predictive Interoception",
        "## Relevance to Internal Movement Arts",
        "## Guardian Interface Links"
      ],
      "summary": "Interoception is the sensing of the internal physiological state of the body. The insular cortex serves as the primary cortical region for interoceptive processing, integrating signals from visceral organs, cardiovascular system, respiratory tract, and musculoskeletal structures. Interoceptive accuracy predicts emotional regulation capacity, pain sensitivity, and the quality of embodied awareness during somatic practices."
    },
