        "# Polyvagal Theory and Autonomic Hierarchy in Somatic Regulation",
        "## Abstract",
        "## Physiological Mechanisms",
        "### Three-Tiered Autonomic Hierarchy",
        "### Neuroception",
        "### Vagal Brake",
        "## Relevance to Internal Movement Arts",
        "## Guardian Interface Links"
      ],
      "summary": "Polyvagal Theory proposed by Stephen Porges describes the autonomic nervous system as a three-tiered phylogenetic hierarchy governing physiological state, social engagement, and survival response. The theory reframes HRV as a direct index of vagal brake function and provides a framework for understanding how movement practices regulate autonomic state through breath, posture, and social context."
