      "summary": "This node examines the role of muscle spindles and Golgi tendon organs as primary proprioceptive transducers in somatic awareness. Proprioception provides the nervous system with continuous positional and velocity data from musculoskeletal structures. Slow movement practices such as Tai Chi and Qigong place exceptional demand on proprioceptive acuity, training sensitivity of these mechanoreceptors over time."
