      "headings": [
        "# Wu Xing Five Element Theory in Traditional Chinese Medicine",
        "## Abstract",
        "## Five Phase Correspondences",
        "### Wood",
        "### Fire",
        "### Earth",
        "### Metal",
        "### Water",
        "## Generative and Control Cycles",
        "### Sheng Generating Cycle",
        "### Ke Controlling Cycle",
        "## Relevance to Internal Movement Arts",
        "## Guardian Interface Links"
      ],
      "summary": "Wu Xing describes five fundamental phases of transformation governing natural phenomena, physiological function, and pathological change in Traditional Chinese Medicine. The five phases are Wood, Fire, Earth, Metal, and Water. Each phase corresponds to organ systems, emotions, seasons, tissues, sensory organs, and climatic factors. Two primary cycles govern inter-elemental relationships: the Sheng generating cycle and the Ke controlling cycle."
    }
